<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William IV, Grand Duke of Luxembourg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1852">1852</a>–<a href="/years/1912">1912</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William IV was Grand Duke of Luxembourg from 1905 to 1912, the son of Grand Duke Adolphe of the House of Nassau-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weilburg">Weilburg</a>. Having six daughters and no sons, he had the succession law changed in 1907 so that his eldest daughter, Marie-Adélaïde, could succeed him. Illness led him to hand the regency to his wife, Marie Anne of Portugal, in 1908.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-iv-grand-duke-of-luxembourg.jpg" alt="William IV, Grand Duke of Luxembourg" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_IV,_Grand_Duke_of_Luxembourg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
